<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6860" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carpēsĭi</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carpētāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in</i> Hispania
			Tarraconensis, <i>the south-western neighbors of the
				Celtiberi</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 26, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">21, 5, 11</span></i> and 16;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 3, 4, § 19</span></i>. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carpētānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of the
				Carpetani</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 3,
					1, 2, § 6</span></i>
			; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carpētānĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the country of the
				Carpetani</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3, 4, §
		25</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
